{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/159068-questions-before-a-new-game","id":159068,"title":"Questions Before a New Game","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Geist: The Sin-Eaters"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-06-04T08:22:14-07:00","id":159068,"title":"Questions Before a New Game","content":"So one of the things I keep seeing all around regarding Geist is how vague it is. To a degree, I agree; while it's nice to have everything open and free for the player to decide, not giving anything as a suggestion seems... I don't know.<br /> <br /> So, do you have any questions you recommend asking of the group prior to digging into a game? Off the top of my head, the big questions I would offer are<br /> <br /> - Who controls the Geists? Players? GM? Other players?<br /> - Can Geists interact with each other?<br /> - Can players interact with other players' Geists?<br /> - Do Sin Eaters look normal to each other, or do they look like time of death? <br /> <br /> <br /> Any other questions you'd suggest?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3192-baileyborough","name":"baileyborough","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-04T08:30:48-07:00","id":159081,"title":"","content":"<b>What is the premise of your krewe?</b><br /> <br /> Hands down the most important question you could ask. This does not necessarily mean what the mythos and ethos of an eventually formalized krewe would be. It just means: who are the player characters as a group, what brings them together and what do they do together? Ask this <i>before they create their characters.</i> Are they a group of friends or allies of convenience beset by all sides? Are they a street gang out to defend their turf and rule the roost? Are they an alliance of knowledge seeking the mysteries of the dead? If you have a preference for the kinds of stories you'd like to be able to run your characters through, share that yourself. Do you want to tell action stories, mystery stories, interpersonal drama? Are there lots of other Bound around the area, and if so, are they hostile or friendly? Deciding on a unified concept will do a lot to narrow down what you can do with the game and provide inspiration for what stories and characters are appropriate.<br /> <br /> <b>How much influence do geists have on their hosts?</b><br /> <br /> This is much less important. It's worth thinking about, though. Do you want any house rules or custom Synergy discord triggers to represent the desires of your geist clashing with the wishes of your characters? If players play each others' geists, you could also do something like Wraith, where the geist can contribute Willpower or some other resource as a bribe in exchange for doing something to fulfill its alien purpose. The clash between Sin-Eater and geist is a theme that recurs in the book, but which has little to no mechanical representation as it is, and having some idea in mind on how to bring it in can help put it more in the spotlight. On the other hand, is this even a theme you and your players want to explore? If you don't find it particularly interesting, there's no need to bother shoring it up with anything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}